  "explanation": "Range 6 means Ashe hits anything on the board from her corner. Against a melee-only board with no divers, the corner is the hex that takes the longest to reach: every enemy has to chew through Sett, Maokai and Taric, then walk the full diagonal. That is three or four more seconds of Ashe arrows than the centre-back gives you, and her Spirit Rift arrow through the most enemies in a line loves a long diagonal through their clump.\n\nThe centre-back is the safe default; here it is the worse hex because there is nothing to be safe from except distance.",
  "principle": "Long range buys distance; use it when the threat is melee. The default hex is a default, not a rule.",
  "guideLink": "/guides/positioning#counter-positioning",
  "commonMistake": "Centring the carry against every board, including the ones where the corner is strictly better."
}
